    "file_name": "XIN_ENG_20061120.0143.tml",
    "doc_text": "XIN_ENG_20061120.0143\n\nANKARA, Nov. 20 , 2006 (Xinhua)\n\nOIC economic standing committee to meet in Istanbul\n\n\n\n\nThe 22nd meeting of the Standing Committee for Economic and Commercial Cooperation (COMCEC) of the Organization of the Islamic Conference (OIC) will be held in Turkey's largest city of Istanbul on Nov. 21-24, local media reported on Monday.\n\nProjects and issues regarding the improvement of economic and commercial cooperation among OIC member states will be debated during the meeting, the semi-official Anatolia news agency reported.\n\nMoreover, second round of the trade negotiations within the context of Framework Agreement Trade Preferential System (TPSOIC) will take place during the meeting, it added.\n\nMinisters of economy from OIC member states as well as observer countries are expected to participate in the meeting, which will be under the chairmanship of Turkish President Ahmet Necdet Sezer.\n\nCOMCEC is one of the three standing committees established by the Third Islamic Summit Conference held in Mecca and Taif in 1981.\n\nThe committee, which was under the presidency of Turkey since 1984, is mainly responsible for the development and coordination of multilateral economic and commercial cooperation between the member states.",
